@startuml
' bt-view-kind: context
' bt-view-id: story-runtime-core:authority-context
title Story Runtime Core - Authority Context
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

' bt-element-id: world
' bt-element-id: core
' bt-element-id: ai

rectangle "World Engine\nResponsibility: Own and commit live story state\nContract: Calls pure shared contracts\n[[../../../../world-engine/world_engine/story_runtime/governed_runtime_adapters.py source]]" as world
rectangle "Story Runtime Core\nResponsibility: Provide portable domain contracts and deterministic algorithms\nContract: Python package without service authority\n[[../../../../story_runtime_core/__init__.py source]]" as core
rectangle "AI Stack\nResponsibility: Produce proposals using shared semantic contracts\nContract: Proposal-only integration\n[[../../../../ai_stack/story_runtime/player_action_resolution.py source]]" as ai

ai ..> core : "uses semantic models\ncontract: proposal-only values\n[[../../../../ai_stack/story_runtime/player_action_resolution.py source]]"
world ..> core : "uses contracts\ncontract: host retains authority\n[[../../../../world-engine/world_engine/story_runtime/governed_runtime_adapters.py source]]"

legend bottom
Viewpoint: context
Concern: Portable contracts versus live and proposal authorities
Elements expose responsibility, contract and source anchor.
Edges name the interaction or dependency contract.
endlegend
@enduml
